{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Where the [D]air is so pure, and the [G]zephyrs so [Gm]free,
The [D]breezes so [E7]balmy and [A7]light,
That I [D]would not exchange my [G]home on the [Gm]range,
For [D]all of the [A7]cities so [D]bright.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
How [D]often at night when the [G]heavens are [Gm]bright,
